Usage: look [OPTION]... STRING [FILE]

Display lines beginning with STRING.  Performs a binary search, so FILE must be sorted.  With no FILE, a default dictionary is used (not available on Windows, so an explicit FILE is required).

OPTIONS:
  -d, --alphanum       compare only alphanumeric and blanks
  -f, --ignore-case    ignore case when comparing
  -a, --alternative    use alternative dictionary order
  -t, --terminate ARG  terminate string at CHAR
      --version        output version information and exit
      --help           display this help and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
